    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Guards a cursor and restores it when the guard is destroyed. If the guard is destroyed without first calling its <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1CommandLine_1_1ExcursionGuard_1aeb5930ef9d71304eb42417f346f93d7c" kindref="member">cancel</ref> method then the associated cursor&apos;s location is reset to its location at the time this guard was constructed. </para>    </detaileddescription>
